WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.900
This is a deck of cards designed with specific features.

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:08.200
In this case, the cards represent the fourteen Bravais lattices.

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:14.000
At the top of each card, there is an example of an element or compound
that exhibits that structural arrangement.

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:20.040
The image in the center acts as the visual target used by the application,
which I will demonstrate shortly.

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:25.100
At the bottom, the card identifies the Bravais lattice that will be displayed.

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:34.070
For example, this card represents a base-centered orthorhombic lattice.
The card colors also indicate the type of centering.

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:38.280
Purple cards represent base-centered lattices.

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:41.630
Green cards represent face-centered lattices.

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:45.360
Blue cards represent body-centered lattices.

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:48.290
Red cards represent primitive lattices.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:58.000
I will now demonstrate how the application works using an augmented reality tool
that I developed for this purpose.

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:02.580
For a clearer demonstration, I will use only one card at a time.

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:07.190
Here is my device.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:12.050
The image may appear slightly unstable because both cameras are moving,
but the application correctly recognizes the card.

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:18.400
In this example, the application displays a monoclinic lattice.

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:25.460
The lattice parameters are shown next to the three-dimensional model.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:34.160
The three cell lengths are different. The alpha and gamma angles are equal to
ninety degrees, while beta has a different value.

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:40.760
I will now use another card.

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:48.550
This one represents a face-centered orthorhombic lattice.

00:01:48.550 --> 00:01:56.390
When I place the device camera over the card again,
the application recognizes the visual target.

00:01:56.390 --> 00:02:04.050
It then displays the corresponding three-dimensional lattice model
and its structural information.

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:11.310
The models may be difficult to observe steadily in this recording
because of the simultaneous movement of the device and the recording camera.

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:18.680
However, all fourteen cards are loaded in the application
and function correctly.

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:26.470
For a clearer view of every model, the application can also be demonstrated in person.

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:34.380
The project is presented as an educational card deck.
The instructions ask the user to place the application camera over a card.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:43.570
Each card contains information about the Bravais lattice that will be displayed,
along with an example of an element or compound with that structural arrangement.

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:47.710
This is the basic way in which Bravais Net works.
